1
00:00:00,780 --> 00:00:04,850
MINUTES AFTER TAKEOFF, BOTH ENGINES LOST POWER

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,690
155 PEOPLE ON BOARD

3
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:12,810
NO RUNWAY WAS CLOSE ENOUGH. ONLY A RIVER

4
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:15,370
AND THEY HAD LESS THAN 4 MINUTES

5
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:18,650
THIS IS US AIRWAYS FLIGHT 1549

6
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,210
JANUARY 15, 2009

7
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:25,330
AN AIRBUS A320, LAGUARDIA TO CHARLOTTE

8
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:31,450
CAPTAIN “SULLY” SULLENBERGER AND FIRST OFFICER JEFFREY SKILES

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,890
AROUND 3:25 P.M., THEY TOOK OFF

10
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:37,330
THEN THEY HIT A FLOCK OF CANADA GEESE

11
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:41,290
THE FIRST OFFICER SAW THE BIRDS SECONDS BEFORE IMPACT

12
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:45,770
BOTH ENGINES SWALLOWED BIRDS. THRUST DROPPED ALMOST TO NOTHING

13
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:48,650
WITHOUT THRUST, THE PLANE WAS A GLIDER

14
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,250
SULLY TOOK THE CONTROLS

15
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:53,130
SKILES WORKED THE ENGINE RESTART CHECKLIST

16
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:56,650
AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL OFFERED A RUNWAY AT TETERBORO

17
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,610
BUT SULLY KNEW THEY COULD NOT REACH IT

18
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:02,490
ONE PLACE LEFT: THE HUDSON RIVER

19
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:05,290
“BRACE FOR IMPACT”

20
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:07,970
THE FLIGHT ATTENDANTS GOT THE PASSENGERS READY

21
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:11,570
AT ABOUT 3:31 P.M., IT TOUCHED DOWN ON THE HUDSON

22
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:13,930
3½ MINUTES AFTER THE BIRDS

23
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:18,090
THE PLANE STAYED AFLOAT. PASSENGERS CLIMBED ONTO THE WINGS

24
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,810
WITHIN 3 MINUTES, THE FIRST FERRY REACHED THEM

25
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,490
6 MORE BOATS ARRIVED WITHIN 10 MINUTES

26
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:25,130
EVERYONE WAS RESCUED

27
00:01:25,180 --> 00:01:27,730
ALL 155 SURVIVED

28
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,730
INVESTIGATORS FOUND BIRDS IN BOTH ENGINES

29
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:34,410
COULD THE PLANE HAVE TURNED BACK?

30
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:39,210
SIMULATIONS LEFT OUT THE TIME TO REALIZE WHAT HAD HAPPENED

31
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:45,370
WITH ONE THING DIFFERENT, IT COULD HAVE BEEN A TRAGEDY

32
00:01:45,420 --> 00:01:48,970
SKILL, TRAINING, AND QUICK DECISIONS

33
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:51,690
NEXT: THE THAI CAVE RESCUE. FOLLOW

